---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Moving to Andorra from France | Official pathways"
  description="A French move to Andorra: the 2001 convention, official permit types on Govern.ad, documents, banks and housing. Hedged. No invented tax rates."
  path="/moving-to-andorra-from-france"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Moving from France</h1>
    <p>
      The eastern and northern roads are the French approaches. The
      authorisation is still issued in Andorra, under Andorran law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Official letter codes, Law 2/2026 amounts and the English A/B/C/D
        practitioner map are on
        <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
        Her Category A is not official A.1. Use
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Govern.ad</a
        >
        and counsel on both sides of the frontier.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>The 2001 convention</h2>
    <p>
      France is a party, with Spain, to the convention of 14 June 2001 on
      entry, circulation, stay and establishment, published on the
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/ministeris-i-secretaries-d-estat/ministeri-de-justicia-i-interior/convenis-i-normativa/convenis"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Ministry of Justice conventions list</a
      >. The convention is not itself a residence permit.
    </p>

    <h2>Documents the Government currently describes</h2>
    <p>
      The
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball/residencia-i-treball-autoritzacio-inicial"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">A.1 page</a
      >
      allows EU and EEA nationals to present a national identity card instead
      of a passport. France is an EU member state. Criminal-record
      certificates, accommodation, civil status and — for workers — a contract
      remain on the published list. Apostille or legalisation is required for
      foreign official documents. Self-employed J.1 and residence-without-work
      D.1 are separate files; an English map of those routes is on
      <a
        href="https://www.livinginandorra.com/residency_options.html"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Living in Andorra</a
      >, with official codes on
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Convention nationals may see a different renewal path on the official
      renewal pages. Read those pages. The first grant on A.1 is described
      there as one year, with later cycles set out on the same text.
    </p>

    <h2>The French-facing parishes</h2>
    <p>
      Encamp includes Pas de la Casa on the French frontier. Canillo and
      Ordino sit on high valleys that many French visitors already know in
      winter. Everyday administration still gathers in Andorra la Vella. See
      the
      <a href="/parishes">seven parishes</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Tax, banks, property</h2>
    <p>
      French tax residence and Andorran tax residence are not the same
      question as an immigration stamp. See
      <a href="/tax-residence">tax residence</a>
      and the
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/impostos-taxes-i-duana"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">taxes theme on Govern.ad</a
      >. Do not treat a ski-season rumour as a rate.
    </p>
    <p>
      Continue with
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>,
      <a href="/opening-a-bank-account">opening a bank account</a>
      and
      <a href="/buying-property">buying property</a>.
      Named firms:
      <a href="/directory">directory</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave your details if you are considering a move from France."
    source="moving-from-france"
  />
</Base>
